+### [Bounding Volume Extrusion](8410-bounding-volume-extrusion.md)
+Computes tight convex hull bounding volumes for caustic beams to enable efficient rasterization of inscattered light while minimizing fill-rate overhead. Unlike the standard bounding prism method, which approximates bilinear beam sides with planar prisms and suffers from poor accuracy on strongly warped or focused beams, this method constructs a 6-triangle convex hull that tightly encloses the beam geometry. Choose it when tight beam enclosure is required for inscattered light rasterization. [Bounding Volume Extrusion](8410-bounding-volume-extrusion.md)
